  "pages": "pp. 26 (default settings), 29-31 (Modbus RTU protocol, data types), 68-73 (Appendix A Modbus registers)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "All registers are holding registers: read with function 03, write with function 16; function 43/14 reads device identification.",
  "int32 and float values are two registers in little-endian word order (least significant word first, CDAB), as the guide's data-type table states and its -123.45 test example shows. Bytes inside each register are big-endian.",
  "The 'differential' accumulation registers restart from zero each time they are read (or reset).",
  "Left out: DSD bins 2-21 (same pattern), the messaging address, autosend message and interval (data-messaging mode only), configuration code, manufacturing date, product name and the module identification strings.",
  "Air pressure (0x0020) is an additional measurement ordering option in the guide."
 ],
